			<div class="content" id="post-content-4730400">
									

<p>I really want to upvote this SCP&#8230; It’s very well written, every single word makes its own contribution to the overall narrative, which made this SCP really difficult to put down when I started reading. I also like the use of images- they are really well incorporated into the exploration logs, as opposed to having simply been pasted into a pre-existing block of text (which I believe to be the cardinal sin of image use).</p>
<p>However&#8230; when I reached the end, my first thought was ‘is that it?’. This SCP gives very little information about the anomaly to the reader. In fact, there is so little information here that it can even be debated whether this SCP is actually anomalous or not- while extremely unlikely, many people disappearing within a small area could have a perfectly mundane explanation, as could all the other weird things mentioned.</p>
<p>I get that leaving the reader in the dark about certain things can have a positive effect, but there is so much information missing here that it’s difficult to work out what this even is. That may appeal to some readers, but unfortunately doesn’t work for me.</p>
<p>Novote, but I constantly find myself coming back to read this, so I may change my verdict in the future.</p>

