					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quasibenevolence" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5140935); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5140935&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238056" alt="Quasibenevolence" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5140935)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quasibenevolence" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5140935); return false;" >Quasibenevolence</a></span> <span class="odate time_1596690934 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Aug 2020 05:15</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4739817">
									

<p>If you're going to provide no punchline besides &quot;this is weird idk man,&quot; the following would make the story pop:</p>
<p>• A good reason why the pheonomenon was discovered in the first place, with details <em>clearly</em> indicating that the weird stuff/bad things were a component of the thing being studied, giving the reader a clear understanding as to how investigation began in the first place.</p>
<p>• If there are weird or unusal spaces, explicitly state what aspects of the space defy physical laws or don't.</p>
<p>I can't stress that second one enough. Rooms don't have to be on blueprints. If a house has a ton of un-enterable rooms, you'll notice the unused space if you live there &#8212; or even if you just visit it. If the house defies the laws of physics, that's something you need to state up-front, then describe the investigation into the same. If pipes do not have a clear function, there are completely mundane ways of tracking their layout and such should be described. If a substance is unidentified, it should be analyzed and the results should be given because <em>that's the point of a report</em>. It's hard to be made unsettled by a demon house when the incomplete report of its researchers seems far more absurd.</p>
<p>Downvote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
